PHASE 1 - THE JDK, READ FROM THE RUNNER AND FROM THE RUNNING PROCESS
================================================================================

  The JDK this tool runs under is the fact most often assumed and most often
  assumed wrongly, in BOTH directions. AAP 0.4.1 and 0.8.2 warn that a reader who
  assumes the build's 17 for all eight non-Joern tools would be wrong, because the
  harness PRECEDENT exported JAVA_HOME_21 for this runner. That warning is about a
  different provisioning. This one assigns 17, and it says so in its own text.

  Three independent readings, in increasing order of authority:

  (1) THE RUNNER'S OWN TEXT.  It invokes the tool with JAVA_HOME="$JAVA_HOME"
      (line 51), harness/env.sh line 47 sets JAVA_HOME to the Temurin 17 home,
      and the runner's header states the assignment outright at line 8. Quoted
      with line numbers in APPENDIX F.

      $ grep -n 'JAVA_HOME' harness/bin/run-dependency-check.sh   (relevant lines)
           8  # Runs under JAVA_HOME (Temurin 17) — JDK 21 is reserved for Joern.
          43  printf 'jdk             : %s\n' "$JAVA_HOME"
          51  JAVA_HOME="$JAVA_HOME" "$DEPENDENCY_CHECK_HOME/bin/dependency-check.sh" \

      The runner also PRINTS the home it assigned, on its own stdout:
        jdk             : /opt/blitzy-tools/jdk/jdk-17.0.20+8

  (2) THAT JDK, MEASURED DIRECTLY.

      $ . harness/env.sh && "$JAVA_HOME/bin/java" -version
        JAVA_HOME=/opt/blitzy-tools/jdk/jdk-17.0.20+8
        openjdk version "17.0.20" 2026-07-21
        OpenJDK Runtime Environment Temurin-17.0.20+8 (build 17.0.20+8)
        OpenJDK 64-Bit Server VM Temurin-17.0.20+8 (build 17.0.20+8, mixed mode, sharing)
        exit=0

      Reported version string : openjdk version "17.0.20" 2026-07-21
      Major                   : 17

  (3) THE JVM THAT ACTUALLY RAN THE SCAN. Sampled from /proc while the scan was
      in flight, matched on the runner's own --out path so it cannot be another
      clone's process. This is the reading that does not depend on any file
      saying what it intends to do. Full argv in APPENDIX E.

      sampled at   : 2026-08-24T22:38:56+00:00
      pid          : 452914
      /proc/pid/exe: /opt/blitzy-tools/jdk/jdk-17.0.20+8/bin/java
      major implied: 17

      Only the process's executable and argv were read. /proc/*/environ was NOT
      read, deliberately: this host carries GITHUB_TOKEN in the environment and a
      log this pipeline preserves verbatim is the last place it may appear.

  VERDICT.  Observed major 17, from all three readings, agreeing.
  runner-metadata.json records jdk_major = 17 for this tool -> MATCH.
  The AAP's halt rule is a rule about MAJOR misassignment (0.9.2): the build on
  anything but 17, or any Joern invocation on anything but 21. Dependency-Check is
  neither, so its assignment is a property of the provisioned runner, and the
  observed value equals the recorded one. Nothing halts. A patch-level difference
  would have been recorded with both values and the run would continue (0.9.1).

  harness/ENVIRONMENT.md corroborates rather than establishes: its runtime-
  topology table gives 'run-dependency-check.sh | $JAVA_HOME (17)' and it
  concludes 'Dependency-Check --version succeeds under both JDKs; 17 is the
  assignment.' The measurement above stands without it.

  NOT ONE OF THE FOUR HEAP-BOUND JVMS. Those are the jimple2cpg frontend build,
  the importCpg verification load, the Stage 3 Joern runner and the Stage 5 probe
  (AAP 0.5.4). This runner sets no JAVA_OPTS and passes no -Xmx: the argv in
  APPENDIX E carries none, and runner-metadata.json records heap_override.takes_one
  = false. The >= 64 GB rule therefore does not apply here and no heap is claimed.

