================================================================================

  REACH AS CONFIGURED. The runner builds one absolute --scan argument per
  allowlist directory (lines 36-40) and hands all 18 to a single invocation.
  That is this runner's reach, recorded as reach and not as an error, and it
  DIFFERS from the harness precedent, which scanned the whole root with a
  test-path exclusion. The argv in APPENDIX E carries 18 --scan arguments, so
  the configured reach and the executed reach are the same thing here.

  Because the paths handed in are absolute, the tool reports absolute paths:
  every one of the 32 dependencies[].filePath values lies under /opt/spark-src.
  That is why this tool's path base is filesystem-absolute and why the normalizer
  relativizes it against SPARK_SRC (PHASE 5).

